messages:
Alex: Quick sync - finalizing the docs changelog for Thursdayrelease. Main items: structured-output flag, a known issue when streaming + tool-calls truncate final tokens, two snippet fixes (py/js), and a short Dedicated migration note. Anyone on deck for a fast review?

Priya: paste the draft here and I'll do a quick legal/consistency pass.

Alex: pasted below. Summary lines should be <=100 chars. Draft includes: feature flag announcement for structured outputs, known issue with streaming+function-calls (with mitigation), embedding model rename note, and example changes for streaming assembly.

Jonah: Ill take the JS snippet. Which file?

Alex: /docs/sdk/js/streaming.md needs updating it currently assumes consumers can just append chunks. Recommend showing chunk-assembly and a fallback to a non-streaming call when function-calls are used.

Jonah: proposed snippet (will push to PR):

```js
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood();
const stream = client.chat.stream({ model: '<model-name>' });
let parts = [];
for await (const chunk of stream) {
  parts.push(chunk.delta ?? chunk.text);
}
let full = parts.join('');
if (full && !full.endsWith('\n')) {
  // fallback to safe complete
  const fallback = await client.chat.complete({ model: '<model-name>', prompt: full });
  full = fallback.text;
}
```

Jonah: will reference the commit hash in the PR when pushed.

Maria: editorial: use placeholders for model names except in code; add a short "expected behavior" bullet under Known issues with recommended mitigations (e.g., use non-streaming for long function-call flows). Also add a redirect for /models/embeds -> /models/embed-v2 and note vector compatibility.

Alex: good. Two asks before merging: 1) include both py/js small fallbacks inline in the Known issues section; 2) add a one-liner migration note for Dedicated about preserve_runtime flag.

Priya: legal/context note: don't use the word "bug" in public changelog; phrase as "known issue" and provide mitigation steps. Also keep the customer-facing summary optimistic (feature-first).

Jonah: pushed commit ab12f7d and added the JS snippet + a short comment about using the chunk-assembly pattern. PR link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4231 (preview later).

Alex: Priya, can you post the final copy edits after Jonah's commit? I'll add the Dedicated migration blurb: "Dedicated customers: to preserve identical runtime outputs across model upgrades, set preserve_runtime=true in your capacity profile." Keep that 100-char.

Priya: done, edited the staging copy (minor tone/consistency tweaks) and added the redirect entry in _redirects.yaml. Also fixed an internal anchor that was 404ing on staging.

docs-bot: Staging preview created: https://deploy-preview.docs.redwood.ai/1792 (contains changelog, Known issues, and updated SDK snippets) :rocket:

Alex: thank you. Any objections to publishing the Known issue with mitigation? Product wants to announce after merge.

Maria: no objections. Thumbs up. :thumbsup:

Jonah: CI passed on the docs site checks. Pushed the final commit ab12f7d, added a short example for assembly in the streaming guide and referenced the Dedicated note.

Alex: merging PR #4231 now. Thanks to everyone for the quick turn.

docs-bot: PR #4231 merged by Alex changelog live on staging. Release notes scheduled for Thursday morning.
